main.cpp
--cpp98
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ namespace function: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ member function: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ global scope: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [basic.lookup.elab]/1, [namespace.udecl]/1: an elaborated-type-
specifier `struct timespec' in namespace n finds ::timespec through the
using-declaration.  tag_scope took the scope of the using-declaration (n)
as the class's scope and declared a new, incomplete n::timespec ("type
'struct timespec' is still incomplete -- cannot initialize", bin53); it
now uses the scope the class is declared in.  Found from libstdc++'s
__platform_semaphore::_M_try_acquire_until_impl
(cpp11_libstdcxx_header_drops/test_stop_token.desc, through <ctime>).  g++
13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
